---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const p='/equipment/01-01/';
---
<Layout pageTitle="CAD and mask workstation" subtitle="" wide={true} description="Inspect a generic two-pad GDSII witness and verify planar connectivity."><script is:inline>window.layoutModule=import('/equipment/01-01/layout.mjs');</script><article class="equipment" id="layoutstation"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/01-01/">← Equipment 01-01</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#lc-refs">References</a><a href="#lc-proof">Verification</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">01-01 / DESIGN WORKSTATION</p><h2>Two contacts and one missing connection</h2><p class="eq-lede">Use the original retro console to check a simple planar witness. Hide the routing to inspect the contacts, break the bridge, then export and reopen both contacts in GDSII.</p></header>
<div class="lc-cols"><section><p class="eq-meta">01 / WORKSTATION</p><h3>BTS Mask Console Mk I</h3><div id="lc-view" aria-label="Interactive retro workstation with live CRT"></div><small id="lc-model" role="status">Loading metre-scale desk…</small><div class="tools">{[['desk','Whole desk'],['crt','CRT'],['keys','Inspection keys'],['back','Rear I/O']].map(([k,t])=><button id={'lc-'+k}>{t}</button>)}</div><p>Orbit and zoom to inspect. Press the brass PADS key, ROUTE key or CHECK on the virtual desk. The CRT shows the same plan and analysis as the drawing panel.</p></section>
<section><p class="eq-meta">02 / LAYOUT</p><h3>Inspect the planar witness</h3><canvas id="lc-map" width="610" height="310" aria-label="Planar mask layout, contacts, routing and outline"></canvas><div class="tools"><button id="lc-pads" aria-pressed="true">Hide contacts</button><button id="lc-traces" aria-pressed="true">Hide routing</button><button id="lc-outline" aria-pressed="true">Hide outline</button></div><div class="tools"><button id="lc-check" class="run">Check connectivity</button><button id="lc-gap">Remove example bridge centre</button><button id="lc-reset">Reset example</button></div><p id="lc-status" role="status"></p><p id="lc-result" aria-live="polite"></p></section></div>
<section><p class="eq-meta">03 / EXCHANGE</p><h3>Round trip a real GDSII file</h3><div class="tools"><button id="lc-export">Export GDSII</button><button id="lc-report" disabled>Export layout and check report</button></div><label>Reopen the exported GDSII<input id="lc-file" type="file" accept=".gds,.gdsii,application/octet-stream"/></label><p>The binary file uses a flat cell, rectangle BOUNDARY elements, integer database-unit coordinates and shape properties for contact and net IDs. Layer 1 datatypes 1 and 2 mark the contact and routing groups of the same conducting plane. Layer 10 is the non-conductive outline. Layer visibility does not change the electrical analysis or exported geometry. The JSON check report preserves design and check revision; re-importing a bare GDS starts a new local revision at zero.</p><p>Only this restricted planar GDSII subset is accepted, not arbitrary hierarchy, curved polygons, path primitives or PCB data. Tested compatible exchange is with available GDS tooling; mixed-layer design and manufacture are outside scope.</p></section>
<section id="lc-refs"><p class="eq-meta">04 / BASIS</p><h3>Original furniture, established file units</h3><p>This custom station uses fictional workstation hardware, not a branded machine or emulation of KLayout, KiCad or FreeCAD. Its 1,440 × 730 mm desk and 350 × 219 mm active CRT are authored design dimensions, independently checked against GLB bounds. Controls and case details are original property of the mockup. <a href="https://www.klayout.de/doc/code/class_Layout.html">KLayout’s Layout database documentation</a> describes integer geometry and µm per DBU; the example uses 0.001 µm (1 nm). The linked <a href="/simulations/interface-designer/">Interface Designer</a> is a separate tool; no compatibility with its internal schema is implied.</p><div class="tools"><a href={p+'build-model.py'} download>Editable Blender source</a><a href={p+'mask-console.glb'} download>Download GLB</a><a href={p+'xr.json'}>Geometry and VR targets</a><a href={p+'layout.mjs'}>Station and GDS code</a><a href={p+'example-intact.gds'} download>Intact GDSII</a><a href={p+'example-open.gds'} download>Broken GDSII</a></div><p>Metric mesh names and separate actions provide reusable ray targets for a VR workshop. This first-pass page is pointer/orbit, not a verified headset session.</p></section>
<section id="lc-proof"><p class="eq-meta">05 / VERIFICATION</p><h3>A file can be valid and its circuit open</h3><p>Axis-aligned rectangles on the same conductive plane connect if they share area or a finite edge; a single point does not count. Components track declared nets so an accidental connection gives a short. A trace rectangle narrower than 1 µm flags an illustrative rule. No foundry rules, corner process limits, multilayer/via extraction, parasitics or biological designs.</p><div class="over"><table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Computed</th><th>Tolerance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Pad identity, binary GDSII round trip</th><td>P1, P2</td><td>P1, P2</td><td>Exact</td></tr><tr><th>Contact spacing (independent gdstk 0.9.61 readback)</th><td>40.000 µm</td><td>40.000 µm</td><td>1 DBU (0.001 µm)</td></tr><tr><th>Bridge intact</th><td>Connected</td><td>Pass</td><td>Exact topology</td></tr><tr><th>2 µm gap</th><td>Open</td><td>Open flagged</td><td>Exact topology</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><a href={p+'external-gds-check.json'}>Independent parser report</a> · <a href={p+'example-report.json'}>Example numerical report</a>. The gdstk check independently reads IDs, units and rectangles. The browser verifies the continuity rules separately.</p></section>
</article></Layout><script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/01-01/client.mjs';</script><style is:global>
#layoutstation .lc-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.13fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:.8rem}#layoutstation section{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:1rem;margin:.85rem 0;min-width:0}#layoutstation .lc-cols section{margin:0}#layoutstation .eq-meta{margin:0}#layoutstation h3{margin:.3rem 0 .6rem;font-size:1.5rem}#layoutstation .tools{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:.45rem;margin:.65rem 0}#layoutstation button,#layoutstation input{min-height:40px;padding:.35rem;box-sizing:border-box;max-width:100%;background:var(--panel,transparent);color:var(--text);border:1px solid var(--border);font:inherit}#layoutstation button{cursor:pointer}#layoutstation button.run{background:#335e50;color:white}#layoutstation button:disabled{opacity:.45}#layoutstation label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.3rem}#lc-view{height:clamp(260px,31vw,405px);background:#2e3535}#lc-view canvas{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;touch-action:none}#lc-map{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}#layoutstation table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}#layoutstation th,#layoutstation td{text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.45rem}#layoutstation .over{overflow:auto}#lc-result{font-weight:bold}@media(max-width:760px){#layoutstation .lc-cols{grid-template-columns:1fr}#layoutstation section{padding:.7rem}}
</style>
